      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T20:43:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is that possible? Looking at `soong_ui.bash --build-mode` gives me the following:\n\n```\nsoong_ui --build-mode --dir\u003d\u003cpath\u003e \u003cbuild action\u003e [\u003cbuild arg 1\u003e \u003cbuild arg 2\u003e ...]\n\nIn build mode, build the set of modules based on the specified build\naction. The --dir flag is required to determine what is needed to\nbuild in the source tree based on the build action. See below for\nthe list of acceptable build action flags.\n```\n\nThe script seems to operate at the module level, where we want to operate at the ninja action node level. For example an entry in the `rust-target-mapping.json`:\n\n```\n{\n  \"name\": \"check_rust\",\n  \"build_target\": \"out/soong/.intermediates/build/soong/scripts/check_rust/check_rust/linux_glibc_x86_64/check_rust\",\n  \"check_target\": \"out/soong/.intermediates/build/soong/scripts/check_rust/check_rust/linux_glibc_x86_64/check_rust.checkJson\",\n  \"source_dir\": \"build/soong/scripts/check_rust\"\n}\n```\n\nCurrently we invoke `out/soong/.intermediates/build/soong/scripts/check_rust/check_rust/linux_glibc_x86_64/check_rust.checkJson` in ninja, I don\u0027t think I can do that in `soong_ui.bash` (at least from what I can see).",
