      "writtenOn": "2025-01-24T14:34:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, running with `--make-mode` is working, but it can trigger a regeneration of the `build.ninja` file and parsing of make modules. Even if it doesn’t we are still checking Android.bp files to see if we need a regeneration of `build.ninja`. This adds an unacceptable overhead to what will be called in a onsave and onload IDE hook. We want this to be analogous to `compile_commands.json` where we give a snapshot of the build parameters at a point in time. `clangd` simply processes the `compile_commands.json` and does not attempt to see if there are any build parameter modifications. If you add files, or change compile flags, etc the developer will need to manually trigger a regeneration of the `build.ninja`/`compile_commands.json` with a `m nothing`.",
      "parentUuid": "9f0bf179_2cd4bd43",
      "revId": "c0b190a88cfa679e1ad17d0b0fc7134e27135f17",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
